>There are many kinds of amulets, and the shape of them is chosen by random
>for every game. You could have identified your stuff to see what it was 
>when you died, now we have no way to tell it. (Except that it wasn't an
>amulet of life saving, since you died WHILE wearing it.)
>There are amulets of:
>
>strangulation (you'll surely know this one when you wear it!)
>change  (changes your alignment)
>ESP (lets you see monsters behind walls if you are close enough,
>	and gives you telepathy)
>life saving (saves you from death once and gets destroyed in the process)
>magical breathing (lets you walk under water)
>amulet vs. poison (you are poison resistant while wearing it)
>
>and, of course, the Amulet of Yendor, but there's only one of these in the
>game and this one wasn't it.
>
>There may be more amulets, but these are the ones I remember without looking
>at the spoilers.

Cursed amulet of restful sleep comes to mind. Urrrrrrrgh. (you just fall asleep
